    "result_text": "Tests are green. I agreed with the finding and addressed it.\n\n**What I changed:** Extracted a new package-private helper `OwnerCityCount.sharingCity(OwnerRepository, String city)` \u2014 modeled directly on `OwnerDailyCount` \u2014 that holds the null-safe, trimmed, case-insensitive city-matching predicate in one place. Both `RejectCityAtCapacity` (hard reject at \u226550) and `FlagCityCapacityWarning` (warn at 40\u201349) now call it, keeping their respective thresholds local while the matching rule has a single home. I also dropped the now-unnecessary \"counts the same way `RejectCityAtCapacity` counts\" javadoc assertion, replacing it with a reference to the shared helper.\n\nThe finding was valid: the codebase deliberately centralizes the reject/flag count predicate for registration dates in `OwnerDailyCount`, and my original version reintroduced exactly the two-places duplication that convention avoids. `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing \u2014 acceptance behaviour unchanged.",
